{"paper": "SSC-CPO-Tier1-04-Oct-2023-Shift1.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 50, "tagged_count": 50, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "The total surface area of a square-based right pyramid is 1536 m2, of which 37.5% is the area of the base of the pyramid. What is the volume (in m3) of this pyramid?", "options": [{"text": "3048", "added": false}, {"text": "3072", "added": false}, {"text": "3144", "added": false}, {"text": "3108", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "frustum-prism-pyramid", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "If sin A+ sin2 A = 1 , then the value of cos4 A + cos6 A is:", "options": [{"text": "cos A", "added": false}, {"text": "sin A", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "ratios-and-tables", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "The radius of a circle is 1.75 cm. What is the circumference of the circle?", "options": [{"text": "5.5 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "11 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "9.63 cm", "added": false}, {"text": "22 cm", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "circle-theorems", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "Let the HCF of m and n be ‘a’ and let n = ab, LCM of m and n is given by:", "options": [{"text": "bm", "added": false}, {"text": "am", "added": false}, {"text": "ab", "added": false}, {"text": "mn", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "720", "added": false}, {"text": "840", "added": false}, {"text": "780", "added": false}, {"text": "820", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "pie-chart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "328.6", "added": false}, {"text": "323.4", "added": false}, {"text": "314.3", "added": false}, {"text": "340.5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cone", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "A sum of money was invested at 10% interest per year, compounded half-yearly, for 18 months. If the amount payable on maturity was ₹64,827, what was the sum invested?", "options": [{"text": "₹55,600", "added": false}, {"text": "₹56,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹56,800", "added": false}, {"text": "₹56,500", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "compounding-frequency", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "Let C be a circle with centre O and radius 5 cm. Let PQ be a tangent to the circle and A be the point of tangency. Let B be a point on PQ such that the length of AB is 12 cm. If the line joining O and B intersects the circle at R, find the length of BR (in cm).", "options": [{"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "13", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "tangents-and-chords", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "When A alone does a piece of work, he takes 25 days more than the time taken by A and B to do the work together. On the other hand, B alone takes 16 days more than the time taken by A and B to do the work together. How many days will A and B, working together, take to do the work?", "options": [{"text": "24", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "23", "added": false}, {"text": "22", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "In what proportion should a grocer mix wheat at ₹12 per kg and ₹25 per kg so as to make a mixture of worth ₹20 per kg?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mixture-Alligation", "sub": "mixture-price", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "Find the mean proportional between 32 and 162.", "options": [{"text": "99", "added": false}, {"text": "65", "added": false}, {"text": "72", "added": false}, {"text": "97", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "Rakhi purchased a basket, a wallet and a belt. She got discounts of 5%, 8% and 10% on the basket, the wallet and the belt, respectively, on their respective marked prices of ₹80, ₹150 and ₹350. How much amount (in ₹) did she pay in total?", "options": [{"text": "529", "added": false}, {"text": "51", "added": false}, {"text": "580", "added": false}, {"text": "519", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "In ΔABC, ∠B = 90° and AB : BC = 1 : 2. The value of cos A + tan C is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "complementary-angles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "The product of two numbers is 20000. If their LCM is 800, then what is their HCF?", "options": [{"text": "25", "added": false}, {"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "35", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "48", "added": false}, {"text": "81", "added": false}, {"text": "27", "added": false}, {"text": "47", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "expression-values", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "3 : 7", "added": false}, {"text": "2 : 3", "added": false}, {"text": "3 : 5", "added": false}, {"text": "2 : 5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "pie-chart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "−1", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "complementary-angles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "The volume of a sphere is given by 130977 cm3. Its surface area (in cm2) is:", "options": [{"text": "16847", "added": false}, {"text": "12474", "added": false}, {"text": "17424", "added": false}, {"text": "14274", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "The speed of a boat in standing water is 6 km/h and the speed of the stream is 2.5 km/h. A man rows to a place at a distance of 59.5 kilometres and comes back to the starting point. The total time taken by him is:", "options": [{"text": "16 hours", "added": false}, {"text": "24 hours", "added": false}, {"text": "22 hours", "added": false}, {"text": "18 hours", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Boats-Streams", "sub": "upstream-downstream", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "The table below shows the number of students commuting to school by different modes of transport: Which mode of transport is used by maximum number of students?", "options": [{"text": "Bicycle", "added": false}, {"text": "Walking", "added": false}, {"text": "Other vehicles", "added": false}, {"text": "School bus", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "A boat covers a distance of 72 km downstream in 6 hours, while it takes 12 hours to cover the same distance upstream. What is the speed of the boat in still water?", "options": [{"text": "6 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "9 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "10 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "8 km/h", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Boats-Streams", "sub": "still-water-and-stream-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "In an election between two candidates, 80% of the voters cast their votes, out of which 5% votes were declared invalid. A candidate got 9500 votes which were 80% of the valid votes. Find the total number of voters enrolled in that election.", "options": [{"text": "14780", "added": false}, {"text": "15100", "added": false}, {"text": "15625", "added": false}, {"text": "16100", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 26, "text": "An inlet pipe can fill an empty tank in 3.6 hours, while an outlet pipe can drain a completely-filled tank in 6.3 hours. If both the pipes are opened simultaneously when the tank is empty, in how many hours will the tank get completely filled?", "options": [{"text": "9.0", "added": false}, {"text": "8.4", "added": false}, {"text": "8.1", "added": false}, {"text": "8.7", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Pipes-Cisterns", "sub": "combined-pipes", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 27, "text": "Avi sold a house to Bhargav at a gain of 10% and Bhargav sold it to Chetan at a gain of 20%. If Chetan paid ₹2,64,00,000 for it, then at what price must Avi have purchased it?", "options": [{"text": "₹2,00,00,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹2,30,00,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹2,50,00,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,75,00,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 28, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "500", "added": false}, {"text": "600", "added": false}, {"text": "650", "added": false}, {"text": "550", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "pie-chart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 29, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 30, "text": "If k(tan 45° sin 60°) = cos 60 ° cot 30 ° , then the value of k is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "ratios-and-tables", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 31, "text": "An inspector is 288 metres behind a thief. The inspector runs 42 metres and the thief runs 30 metres in a minute. In how much time will the inspector catch the thief?", "options": [{"text": "24 minutes", "added": false}, {"text": "19 minutes", "added": false}, {"text": "21 minutes", "added": false}, {"text": "20 minutes", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "relative-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 32, "text": "Three boys, on an average, are 25 years old, and their age are in the ratio of 3 : 5 : 7. What is the age of youngest boy'?", "options": [{"text": "24 years", "added": false}, {"text": "21 years", "added": false}, {"text": "12 years", "added": false}, {"text": "15 years", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ages", "sub": "ratio-of-ages", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 33, "text": "Two numbers are in the ratio 12:7. If their HCF is 25, find the numbers.", "options": [{"text": "225, 135", "added": false}, {"text": "300, 175", "added": false}, {"text": "300, 50", "added": false}, {"text": "175, 120", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 34, "text": "A dealer sells his goods at 10% loss on the cost price but uses 25% less weight. What is his profit percentage?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 35, "text": "A and B undertake a project worth ₹36,000. A alone can do the work in 25 days. They worked together for 5 days. For the next five days, B worked alone. After that, A substituted B and completed the remaining work in 5 days. The share of A in the earnings is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 36, "text": "A shopkeeper has a sale of ₹5,445, ₹5,937, ₹5,865 and ₹6,562 for 4 consecutive days. If he gets an average sale of ₹6,050 for 5 days, then his sale on the fifth day is:", "options": [{"text": "₹6,131", "added": false}, {"text": "₹6,341", "added": false}, {"text": "₹6,441", "added": false}, {"text": "₹6,231", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "series-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 37, "text": "Study the given table and answer the question that follows. The data given in the table is for the month of December 2022. What is the difference between the number of male employees in company P and that in company R?", "options": [{"text": "592", "added": false}, {"text": "578", "added": false}, {"text": "605", "added": false}, {"text": "580", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 38, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1,10,000", "added": false}, {"text": "80,000", "added": false}, {"text": "1,00,000", "added": false}, {"text": "1,20,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 39, "text": "A company is manufacturing boxes of three types – plastic, wood and glass. The ratio of the numbers of plastic, wood and glass boxes is 2 : 3 : 5. The difference between the numbers of wood and glass boxes is 144. If the number of plastic boxes is increased by 25%, then what will be the number of plastic boxes now?", "options": [{"text": "144", "added": false}, {"text": "360", "added": false}, {"text": "216", "added": false}, {"text": "180", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 40, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 41, "text": "After deducing a commission of 20%, a DVD set costs ₹9,080. Its marked price is:", "options": [{"text": "₹11,200", "added": false}, {"text": "₹11,350", "added": false}, {"text": "₹10,000", "added": false}, {"text": "₹10,100", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 42, "text": "Anandi bought a smart watch from an electronic store for Rs.4,400. Since she had less money, she paid Rs.2,000 for down payment and the shopkeeper offered her an alternative to pay Rs.2,440 after 1 month. Find the rate of interest being charged at simple interest by the shopkeeper in this instalment option?", "options": [{"text": "20%", "added": false}, {"text": "10%", "added": false}, {"text": "22%", "added": false}, {"text": "15%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-instalments", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 43, "text": "PQR is a triangle. The bisectors of the internal angle ∠Q and external angle ∠R intersect at S. If ∠ QSR = 40°, then ∠P is:", "options": [{"text": "40°", "added": false}, {"text": "60°", "added": false}, {"text": "80°", "added": false}, {"text": "30°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 2D", "sub": "circle-sector-ring", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 44, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "2", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 45, "text": "The given table shows the number of students from 4 schools during 2022-2023. What is the percentage of girls in school B?", "options": [{"text": "65%", "added": false}, {"text": "45%", "added": false}, {"text": "60%", "added": false}, {"text": "55%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 46, "text": "E, F, G, and H are four points lying on the circumference of a circle to make a cyclic quadrilateral. If ∠FGH = 57°, then what will be the measure of the ∠HEF?", "options": [{"text": "33°", "added": false}, {"text": "123°", "added": false}, {"text": "93°", "added": false}, {"text": "143°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Circles-Polygons", "sub": "cyclic-quadrilaterals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 47, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "roots", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 48, "text": "If the radius of a hemispherical balloon increases from 4 cm to 7 cm as air is pumped into it, find the ratio of the surface area of the new balloon to its original.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "frustum-prism-pyramid", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 49, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "32 AH", "added": false}, {"text": "35 AH", "added": false}, {"text": "4 AH", "added": false}, {"text": "55 AH", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 50, "text": "Study the given table and answer the question that follows. The table shows the number of students studying in 6 different classes of 6 different schools. Which class has the maximum number of students from all schools together?", "options": [{"text": "X", "added": false}, {"text": "VII", "added": false}, {"text": "VI", "added": false}, {"text": "V", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}]}